stage_instructions.calculator:
At this stage you send a private calculator request, and the host returns the calculation result afterward. Return the literal JSON null to skip. Otherwise use exactly this request shape
{"candidate_contributions": [C1, C2], "assumed_other_contributions": PARTNERS}
Replace C1 and C2 with 2 distinct JSON integers from 0 through 20. Replace PARTNERS with null or an array of 3 JSON integers from 0 through 20. Do not output the placeholder names. The partner vector follows player_order excluding you and remains a hypothetical assumption, not an observation of simultaneous current choices. Return only the request fields, without payoff fields or a completed ledger. Records in STATE are context, not response templates for this stage. Calculator candidates do not restrict your final contribution.
